=====ASSETS README=====
# Assets

Reusable components shared across lessons. **Reuse is the default.** Read this
directory before writing a lesson; add anything a second lesson could use here
rather than inlining it.

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `course.css` | Shared stylesheet. Every lesson and reference doc links it. Tufte-influenced, print-clean. |

## Components in `course.css`

- `.callout` — with `--field` (do this at practice) and `--myth` (common wrong belief) variants
- `.cite` — inline citation block; `.primary-source` — the one source per lesson
- `.constraint-performer` / `--task` / `--environment` — colour-coded table rows for the three constraint classes. Keep these colours consistent across every lesson.
- `.continuum` — control → chaos progression bar
- `.quiz` — retrieval-practice widget. Per the teach skill, **every option must be the same length** so formatting gives nothing away.

## Still to build

- `quiz.js` — the behaviour behind `.quiz`. First lesson with a quiz earns it.
- A drill-diagram helper (SVG field with player positions) once lessons need one.
